## The first ecological assessment of Culcita sp. in the Gulf of Thailand reveals shifts in dietary selectivity under elevated Acanthaster sp. densities. 

Repository accompanying publication:

The first ecological assessment of Culcita sp. in the Gulf of Thailand reveals shifts in dietary selectivity under elevated Acanthaster sp. densities. 

## Authors

Bjarne Deram
Scarlett R. Taylor
Stephanie W. Topal
Jessica Miles
Piers Baillie
Gavin Miller

## Contents

- Raw datasets
- R scripts including:
      - Statistical analyses
      - Figure generation

## Reproducing the analyses

All scripts can be run independently and do not impact each others analysis. 

## Software

R version 4.4.2

Packages needed are written out in each script. 


